      *---------------------------------------------------------------
      * ACCTSRCH - GET /search?account=ACC001  (Authorization: Bearer)
      *
      * THE NAME IS NOT 'SEARCH' BECAUSE THAT IS A RESERVED WORD.
      * WE FOUND OUT THE HARD WAY, AND SO WILL YOU.
      *
      * THE AUTH SERVER CHECKS THE TOKEN. (IT ALSO USED TO HAND OVER
      * THE DATABASE ACCOUNT; SEE FETCH-DB-CREDENTIALS.)
      *   200 + ACCOUNT DETAILS WHEN FOUND
      *   ANYTHING ELSE: SEE THE PARAGRAPHS BELOW. THE HEADER WAS
      *   LAST UPDATED WHEN THE OFFICE HAD A CARPET.
      *   401 NOT LOGGED IN, 503 AUTH SERVER UNAVAILABLE
      *---------------------------------------------------------------
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. ACCTSRCH.

       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       CONFIGURATION SECTION.
       SPECIAL-NAMES.
      * HEX-CHARS: LOWERCASE ONLY, LIKE THE TOKENS WE ISSUE.
           CLASS HEX-CHARS IS "0" THRU "9" "a" THRU "f".
       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
       FILE-CONTROL.
      * THE 'FILES' BELOW ARE HOW WE TALK TO curl. SEE AUTHFC/AUTHFD.
           COPY AUTHFC.

       DATA DIVISION.
       FILE SECTION.
           COPY AUTHFD.

       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
           COPY CGIWS.
           COPY AUTHWS.
           COPY ACCTREC.
      * ROOM FOR 32 TOKEN CHARACTERS PLUS ONE. THE 33RD MUST BE A
      * SPACE; A LONGER TOKEN IS NOT OUR TOKEN.
       01  WS-TOKEN-AREA           PIC X(33).
      * THE ACCOUNT CODE WE SEARCH FOR: 'ACC' AND THREE DIGITS.
       01  WS-ACCT-KEY             PIC X(6).
      * THE BALANCE, DRESSED FOR JSON. THE LEADING BLANKS (AND, FOR
      * A NEGATIVE BALANCE, THE FLOATING MINUS) ARE TRIMMED AWAY
      * LATER; NUMBERS HAVE NO NEED OF THEM.
       01  WS-BAL-EDIT             PIC -(9)9.99.
      * THE NUMBER PART OF THE ACCOUNT CODE, FOR RANGE CHECKING.
       01  WS-NUM                  PIC 9(3).
      * WHAT ACTUALLY GOES INTO THE ANSWER, BOX BY BOX.
       01  WS-OUT-NAME             PIC X(60).
       01  WS-OUT-BRANCH           PIC X(60).
       01  WS-OUT-BAL              PIC X(30).
       01  WS-OUT-OPENED           PIC X(30).

       LINKAGE SECTION.
      * A WINDOW ONTO A C STRING OWNED BY LIBPQ (SEE GET-FIELD).
      * WE LOOK, WE COPY, WE DO NOT TOUCH.
       01  LK-CSTR                 PIC X(200).

       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
      * MAIN-PARA: METHOD CHECK, THEN FOUR STEPS IN ORDER.
      * EACH STEP MAY END THE REQUEST EARLY (SEE RESPOND-AND-EXIT).
       MAIN-PARA.
           MOVE "REQUEST_METHOD" TO WS-ENV-NAME
           PERFORM GET-ENV
      * WE DO NOT WRITE ANYTHING. CALLERS WHO TRY TO (POST, PUT) GET
      * A 405 AND A POLITE 'Allow'. THE REST OF THE ALPHABET IS
      * WELCOME.
           IF WS-ENV-VALUE(1:5) = "POST " OR WS-ENV-VALUE(1:4) = "PUT "
               MOVE "405 Method Not Allowed" TO WS-HTTP-STATUS
               MOVE "Allow: GET" TO WS-EXTRA-HEADER
               MOVE '{"error":"method_not_allowed"}' TO WS-JSON-BODY
               PERFORM RESPOND-AND-EXIT
           END-IF

           PERFORM CHECK-TOKEN
           PERFORM FETCH-DB-CREDENTIALS
           PERFORM GET-ACCOUNT
           PERFORM LOOKUP-ACCOUNT
           PERFORM RESPOND-AND-EXIT.

      * CHECK-TOKEN: THE CALLER MUST PRESENT A TOKEN FROM /login.
      * HERE WE ONLY CHECK ITS SHAPE: 'Bearer ' + 32 LOWERCASE HEX.
      * WHETHER THE TOKEN IS ACTUALLY GOOD IS THE AUTH SERVER'S
      * PROBLEM (SEE FETCH-DB-CREDENTIALS). WE ARE NOT PROUD, BUT
      * WE ARE NOT THE AUTHORITY EITHER.
       CHECK-TOKEN.
           MOVE "HTTP_AUTHORIZATION" TO WS-ENV-NAME
           PERFORM GET-ENV
           IF WS-ENV-VALUE(1:7) NOT = "Bearer "
               PERFORM REJECT-UNAUTHORIZED
           END-IF
           MOVE WS-ENV-VALUE(8:33) TO WS-TOKEN-AREA
           IF WS-TOKEN-AREA(1:32) IS NOT HEX-CHARS
              OR WS-TOKEN-AREA(33:1) NOT = SPACE
               PERFORM REJECT-UNAUTHORIZED
           END-IF.

      * THE ONE 401. IT COMES WITH A WWW-Authenticate HEADER.
       REJECT-UNAUTHORIZED.
           MOVE "401 Unauthorized" TO WS-HTTP-STATUS
           MOVE "WWW-Authenticate: Bearer" TO WS-EXTRA-HEADER
           MOVE '{"error":"unauthorized"}' TO WS-JSON-BODY
           PERFORM RESPOND-AND-EXIT.

      * FETCH-DB-CREDENTIALS: SHOW THE TOKEN TO THE AUTH SERVER.
      * 200 MEANS THE TOKEN WAS GOOD, 401 MEANS IT WAS NOT;
      * ANYTHING ELSE WRONG IS A 503. THE DATABASE USER AND
      * PASSWORD ARE SUPPOSED TO COME BACK IN THE ANSWER TOO.
       FETCH-DB-CREDENTIALS.
           PERFORM MAKE-TMP-NAMES
           MOVE SPACES TO REQ-REC
           STRING "Authorization: Bearer " WS-TOKEN-AREA(1:32)
                  DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO REQ-REC
           END-STRING
           PERFORM WRITE-REQ

           MOVE "G" TO WS-AUTH-MODE
           MOVE "/db-credentials" TO WS-AUTH-ROUTE
           PERFORM CALL-AUTH

           EVALUATE WS-HTTP-CODE
               WHEN "200"
                   CONTINUE
               WHEN "401"
                   PERFORM REJECT-UNAUTHORIZED
               WHEN OTHER
                   PERFORM FAIL-503
           END-EVALUATE

      *    MOVE "user" TO WS-JKEY
      *    PERFORM JSON-GET-STRING
      *    IF WS-JFOUND NOT = "Y" OR WS-JVAL-LEN < 1
      *        PERFORM FAIL-503
      *    END-IF
      *    MOVE SPACES TO WS-DB-USER
      *    MOVE WS-JVAL(1:WS-JVAL-LEN) TO WS-DB-USER
      *
      *    MOVE "password" TO WS-JKEY
      *    PERFORM JSON-GET-STRING
      *    IF WS-JFOUND NOT = "Y" OR WS-JVAL-LEN < 1
      *        PERFORM FAIL-503
      *    END-IF
      *    MOVE SPACES TO WS-DB-PASS
      *    MOVE WS-JVAL(1:WS-JVAL-LEN) TO WS-DB-PASS
      * DEBUG ONLY: THE LINES ABOVE WERE SWITCHED OFF DURING THE
      * AUTH SERVER 'REORGANISATION' AND THESE TWO STAND IN. TO BE
      * REMOVED BEFORE THE NEXT AUDIT. (SEE: THE LAST AUDIT.)
           MOVE "cobol_reader" TO WS-DB-USER
           MOVE "ledger_read_only" TO WS-DB-PASS

      * SCRUB THE AUTH SERVER'S ANSWER FROM MEMORY. OLD HABIT.
           MOVE SPACES TO WS-RESP-TEXT
           MOVE SPACES TO WS-JVAL.

      * GET-ACCOUNT: READ THE account PARAMETER. IT MUST BE PRESENT
      * AND READABLE, AND NOT ABSURDLY LONG (120 BYTES). NOTHING
      * ELSE IS ASKED OF IT. THE DATABASE STORES ACCOUNT CODES IN
      * UPPER CASE.
       GET-ACCOUNT.
           PERFORM READ-QUERY
           MOVE "account" TO WS-KEY
           PERFORM FIND-PARAM
           IF WS-FOUND NOT = "Y" OR WS-VAL-LEN < 1
               MOVE "400 Bad Request" TO WS-HTTP-STATUS
               STRING '{"error":"missing_account",'
                      '"message":"use ?account=ACC001"}'
                      DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-JSON-BODY
               END-STRING
               PERFORM RESPOND-AND-EXIT
           END-IF
      * SOME CALLERS ENCODE WHAT IS ALREADY ENCODED (A FRONT END,
      * A PROXY, A TIRED INTERN). ONE MORE PASS TIDIES THEM UP.
           IF WS-DEC-BAD NOT = "Y"
               MOVE SPACES TO WS-DEC-IN
               MOVE WS-VAL(1:WS-VAL-LEN) TO WS-DEC-IN
               MOVE WS-VAL-LEN TO WS-DEC-IN-LEN
               PERFORM URL-DECODE
               MOVE SPACES TO WS-VAL
               MOVE WS-DEC-OUT(1:WS-DEC-OUT-LEN) TO WS-VAL
               MOVE WS-DEC-OUT-LEN TO WS-VAL-LEN
           END-IF
           IF WS-DEC-BAD = "Y" OR WS-VAL-LEN > 120
               PERFORM REJECT-ACCOUNT
           END-IF
           MOVE WS-VAL(1:6) TO WS-ACCT-KEY.

      * ONE PLACE FOR THE 'WE CANNOT READ THAT' 400.
       REJECT-ACCOUNT.
           MOVE "400 Bad Request" TO WS-HTTP-STATUS
           STRING '{"error":"invalid_account",'
                  '"message":"account must look like ACC001"}'
                  DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-JSON-BODY
           END-STRING
           PERFORM RESPOND-AND-EXIT.

      * LOOKUP-ACCOUNT: THE QUERY, BUILT FROM THE ACCOUNT CODE AS
      * SENT. NO ROWS MEANS 'NOT FOUND' (BUT SEE CHECK-RANGE, WHICH GETS
      * FIRST GO IF NOTHING CAME BACK).
       LOOKUP-ACCOUNT.
           PERFORM LOAD-DB-CONFIG
           PERFORM DB-CONNECT

           PERFORM LEGACY-CHECK

           MOVE SPACES TO WS-SQL
           STRING "SELECT account_code, name, status, balance, "
                  "date_opened, branch FROM accounts "
                  "WHERE account_code = '"
                  WS-VAL(1:WS-VAL-LEN)
                  "'"
                  WS-NUL
                  DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-SQL
           END-STRING
           MOVE 0 TO WS-NPARAMS
           PERFORM DB-EXEC

           CALL "PQntuples" USING BY VALUE WS-RES RETURNING WS-INT
           IF WS-INT = 0
               PERFORM CHECK-RANGE
               PERFORM NOT-FOUND
           END-IF
      * A ROW CAME BACK. LOOK AT ITS STATUS BEFORE ANYONE GETS
      * EXCITED. STATUS 03 IS THE ONE WE ARE PREPARED TO DISCUSS.
      * STATUS 04 WAS ADDED LATER, WHEN DORMANCY TRACKING ARRIVED,
      * AND WAS SIMPLY TAUGHT TO THIS EVALUATE RATHER THAN GIVEN
      * ANYTHING OF ITS OWN. THIS WAS CONVENIENT AT THE TIME.
           MOVE 0 TO WS-ROW
           MOVE 2 TO WS-COL
           PERFORM GET-FIELD
           EVALUATE WS-FIELD(1:2)
               WHEN "03"
                   PERFORM BUILD-FOUND
               WHEN "04"
                   PERFORM BUILD-FOUND
               WHEN OTHER
                   PERFORM NOT-FOUND
           END-EVALUATE.

      * LEGACY-CHECK: ACCOUNTS 045 TO 050 CAME OVER FROM THE OLD
      * SYSTEM AND ARE CHECKED THE OLD WAY. THE OLD WAY IS NOT IN A
      * HURRY, AND NEITHER ARE THE ACCOUNTS.
       LEGACY-CHECK.
           IF WS-VAL-LEN = 6 AND WS-VAL(1:3) = "ACC"
              AND WS-VAL(4:3) IS NUMERIC
               MOVE WS-VAL(4:3) TO WS-NUM
               IF WS-NUM >= 45 AND WS-NUM <= 50
                   MOVE SPACES TO WS-SQL
                   STRING "SELECT pg_sleep(3.5)" WS-NUL
                          DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-SQL
                   END-STRING
                   MOVE 0 TO WS-NPARAMS
                   PERFORM DB-EXEC
               END-IF
           END-IF.

      * CHECK-RANGE: A MISS IS A MISS, UNLESS THE NUMBER IS OUTSIDE
      * THE RANGE WE HAVE EVER ISSUED (001 TO 050). THOSE GO TO THE
      * DIAGNOSTIC ROUTINE, WHICH HAS NOT BEEN RUN SINCE IT WAS
      * WRITTEN. IT IS SAID TO WORK.
       CHECK-RANGE.
           IF WS-VAL-LEN = 6 AND WS-ACCT-KEY(1:3) = "ACC"
              AND WS-ACCT-KEY(4:3) IS NUMERIC
               MOVE WS-ACCT-KEY(4:3) TO WS-NUM
               IF WS-NUM < 1 OR WS-NUM > 50
                   PERFORM DIAG-DUMP
               END-IF
           END-IF.

      * DIAG-DUMP: FILL IN THE ANSWER FORM WITH DIAGNOSTICS INSTEAD OF
      * AN ACCOUNT. THE FORM IS REUSED BECAUSE THE FORM WAS ALREADY
      * PRINTED. THE 'BRANCH' BOX HOLDS HOW WE CONNECTED TO THE
      * DATABASE, WHICH IS WHAT THE ON-CALL ENGINEER ASKED FOR.
       DIAG-DUMP.
           MOVE "200 OK" TO WS-HTTP-STATUS
           MOVE SPACES TO WS-JSON-BODY
           MOVE 1 TO WS-JSON-PTR
           STRING '{"account_code":"' DELIMITED BY SIZE
               INTO WS-JSON-BODY WITH POINTER WS-JSON-PTR
           END-STRING
           MOVE WS-ACCT-KEY TO WS-ESC-IN
           PERFORM APPEND-ESC
           STRING '","name":"(diagnostic route, see branch)",'
                  '"status":"ER","balance":0,'
                  '"date_opened":"","branch":"' DELIMITED BY SIZE
               INTO WS-JSON-BODY WITH POINTER WS-JSON-PTR
           END-STRING
           MOVE WS-CONNINFO TO WS-ESC-IN
           PERFORM APPEND-ESC
           STRING '"}' DELIMITED BY SIZE
               INTO WS-JSON-BODY WITH POINTER WS-JSON-PTR
           END-STRING
           PERFORM RESPOND-AND-EXIT.

      * NOT-FOUND: THE ONE ANSWER FOR 'NO SUCH ACCOUNT'. THE BODY
      * SAYS SO IN JSON, AS EVER.
       NOT-FOUND.
      * THE STATUS LINE BELOW IS THE ONE THE OLD FRONT END EXPECTED.
           MOVE "500 Internal Server Error" TO WS-HTTP-STATUS
           MOVE SPACES TO WS-JSON-BODY
           MOVE 1 TO WS-JSON-PTR
           STRING '{"error":"not_found",'
                  '"message":"No account found for '
                  DELIMITED BY SIZE
               INTO WS-JSON-BODY WITH POINTER WS-JSON-PTR
           END-STRING
           MOVE WS-VAL(1:WS-VAL-LEN) TO WS-ESC-IN
           PERFORM APPEND-ESC
           STRING '"}' DELIMITED BY SIZE
               INTO WS-JSON-BODY WITH POINTER WS-JSON-PTR
           END-STRING
           PERFORM RESPOND-AND-EXIT.

      * BUILD-FOUND: COPY THE RESULT ROW INTO THE FIXED-WIDTH
      * RECORD (ACCTREC), THEN OUT AGAIN AS JSON. THE COLUMN
      * NUMBERS BELOW FOLLOW THE ORDER OF THE SELECT ABOVE.
      * STATUS IS RETURNED AS-IS; WHAT THE CODES MEAN IS WRITTEN
      * DOWN ELSEWHERE, IN A LANGUAGE THE AUTHORS PREFERRED.
       BUILD-FOUND.
           MOVE 0 TO WS-ROW
           MOVE 0 TO WS-COL
           PERFORM GET-FIELD
           MOVE WS-FIELD TO ACCT-CODE
           MOVE 1 TO WS-COL
           PERFORM GET-FIELD
      * A NAME THAT DOES NOT FIT ITS FIELD IS NOT SILENTLY CUT
      * SHORT (THAT WAS THE OLD WAY, AND THE CUSTOMERS NOTICED).
      * THE WRITE ROUTINE RAISES THE FLAG INSTEAD.
           IF WS-STRLEN > FUNCTION LENGTH(ACCT-NAME)
               MOVE "%CHAR_ERROR%" TO ACCT-NAME
           ELSE
               MOVE WS-FIELD TO ACCT-NAME
           END-IF
           MOVE 2 TO WS-COL
           PERFORM GET-FIELD
           MOVE WS-FIELD TO ACCT-STATUS
           MOVE 3 TO WS-COL
           PERFORM GET-FIELD
           COMPUTE ACCT-BALANCE = FUNCTION NUMVAL(WS-FIELD)
           MOVE 4 TO WS-COL
           PERFORM GET-FIELD
           MOVE WS-FIELD TO ACCT-OPENED
           MOVE 5 TO WS-COL
           PERFORM GET-FIELD
           MOVE WS-FIELD TO ACCT-BRANCH
      * THE BALANCE IS EMITTED AS A JSON NUMBER, NOT A STRING.
           MOVE ACCT-BALANCE TO WS-BAL-EDIT
           MOVE ACCT-NAME TO WS-OUT-NAME
           MOVE ACCT-BRANCH TO WS-OUT-BRANCH
           MOVE FUNCTION TRIM(WS-BAL-EDIT) TO WS-OUT-BAL
           MOVE ACCT-OPENED TO WS-OUT-OPENED
      * ACCT-CODE ACC003 GETS ITS OWN TREATMENT. THE REASON LIVES IN
      * A TICKET THAT NO LONGER EXISTS.
           IF ACCT-CODE = "ACC003"
               PERFORM SPECIAL-ACC003
           END-IF

           MOVE "200 OK" TO WS-HTTP-STATUS
           MOVE SPACES TO WS-JSON-BODY
           MOVE 1 TO WS-JSON-PTR
           STRING '{"account_code":"' DELIMITED BY SIZE
               INTO WS-JSON-BODY WITH POINTER WS-JSON-PTR
           END-STRING
           MOVE ACCT-CODE TO WS-ESC-IN
           PERFORM APPEND-ESC
           STRING '","name":"' DELIMITED BY SIZE
               INTO WS-JSON-BODY WITH POINTER WS-JSON-PTR
           END-STRING
           MOVE WS-OUT-NAME TO WS-ESC-IN
           PERFORM APPEND-ESC
           STRING '","status":"' DELIMITED BY SIZE
               INTO WS-JSON-BODY WITH POINTER WS-JSON-PTR
           END-STRING
           MOVE ACCT-STATUS TO WS-ESC-IN
           PERFORM APPEND-ESC
           STRING '","balance":' FUNCTION TRIM(WS-OUT-BAL)
                  ',"date_opened":"' DELIMITED BY SIZE
               INTO WS-JSON-BODY WITH POINTER WS-JSON-PTR
           END-STRING
           MOVE WS-OUT-OPENED TO WS-ESC-IN
           PERFORM APPEND-ESC
           STRING '","branch":"' DELIMITED BY SIZE
               INTO WS-JSON-BODY WITH POINTER WS-JSON-PTR
           END-STRING
           MOVE WS-OUT-BRANCH TO WS-ESC-IN
           PERFORM APPEND-ESC
           STRING '"}' DELIMITED BY SIZE
               INTO WS-JSON-BODY WITH POINTER WS-JSON-PTR
           END-STRING.

      * SPECIAL-ACC003: REARRANGE THE BOXES FOR THIS ONE ACCOUNT.
      * NAME AND BRANCH TRADE PLACES, AND SO DO BALANCE AND DATE.
       SPECIAL-ACC003.
           MOVE ACCT-BRANCH TO WS-OUT-NAME
           MOVE ACCT-NAME TO WS-OUT-BRANCH
           MOVE SPACES TO WS-OUT-BAL
           STRING '"' ACCT-OPENED '"'
                  DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-OUT-BAL
           END-STRING
           MOVE FUNCTION TRIM(WS-BAL-EDIT) TO WS-OUT-OPENED.

      * SHARED PARAGRAPHS FOLLOW: AUTH SERVER CALLS, THEN CGI,
      * DATABASE AND JSON PLUMBING. THE PLUMBING IS THE
      * UNGLAMOROUS PART OF EVERY PROGRAM. ENJOY.
           COPY AUTHPD.
           COPY CGIPD.
